# shir_nodes/err_line.node — ErrLine: write a VALUE to STDERR as one line.
#
# GENERIC. The typed counterpart of a stdout print for the diagnostic
# channel: the operand is formatted by the frontend exactly as a stdout
# print would format it (same `{}`/`{name}` interpolation, same refusal of
# width/precision specs), and the runtime appends the newline. Stdout is
# untouched, so a program that interleaves the two streams keeps each
# stream's own byte order.
#
# The runtime member is `sh2.warn`, the channel the shell frontends
# already use for `>&2` diagnostics — rendered code may only call
# whitelisted `sh2.<name>` members, so the stderr write has to go through
# the namespace rather than a raw `process.stderr.write`.
node ErrLine
tag "ErrLine"
kind expr
field value: expr
# Spec: TextOps#spread_sound is NOT the law here; the obligation is the
# stream separation itself (the value reaches stderr verbatim, once, with
# one trailing newline, and stdout receives nothing). Recorded as a
# node-local contract rather than a TextOps law.
#
# NOT PROMISED (stated, not assumed): the ORDER of this write against
# writes to the OTHER stream beyond what the host guarantees per stream;
# the host's flushing/缓冲 behaviour for a redirected stderr; and anything
# about `{:?}` (Debug formatting is a different renderer, refused by
# frontends that cannot prove it equals Display).
